  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 3-Methylfentanyl and the Kappa-type opioid receptor, as it is indirectly linked through multiple targets. The drug is associated with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, which is a known target of several compounds, including Ginkgolide A and Tepoxalin. These compounds, in turn, target the Kappa-type opioid receptor, indicating a possible pathway through which 3-Methylfentanyl may exert its effects. The scores from the paths are consistent, with a final score of 0.7694, suggesting a strong but not absolute correlation. The evidence highlights the role of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C as a bridge between 3-Methylfentanyl and the Kappa-type opioid receptor, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The findings underscore the importance of receptor-target interactions in drug action, but further research is needed to confirm the direct relationship between 3-Methylfentanyl and the Kappa-type opioid receptor.",
